<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramavati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramavati was a capital of the Pala dynasty founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramapala">Ramapala</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varendra">Varendra</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, after he recovered the region from the Kaivarta rebels in the late eleventh century. It is praised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramacharita">Ramacharita</a> and served as the seat of the last Pala kings, but its exact site has not been securely identified.</p></div>
